      "content": "International law and United Nations resolutions generally acknowledge both the rights of Palestinians to statehood and self-determination while also recognizing the existence of Israel as a sovereign state. For example, the Fourth Geneva Convention, to which Israel is a signatory, prohibits an occupying power from transferring its population into the territory it occupies. Many international actors, including the UN, have called for the cessation of Israeli settlements, viewing them as illegal under international law. The conflict involves indigenous inhabitants (Palestinians) and recent settlers (Jews and Israelis), with historical claims overlapping but not always aligning with international perspectives on self-determination, occupation, and settlement legality. The complexity of the conflict and its legal interpretations make it a subject of prolonged diplomatic and scholarly debate, often viewed through contrasting national, political, and legal lenses.",
